  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes, especially when sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment turns negative (e.g., -0.25 or 0.00) and historical mean reversion is observed.",
    "Apply a lag correction: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast, reduce next period’s forecast by 5–10% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "When sentiment is positive (e.g., 0.33), increase forecast slightly but cap at 10% above recent 7-day average to avoid overconfidence.",
    "If model consistently overpredicts early in the 30-day horizon, apply a 3–5% downward bias to the first 5 days of forecast.",
    "For sentiment = 0.00, use a conservative mean-reversion filter: forecast = 0.9 * previous forecast + 0.1 * 30-day moving average."
  ]
}
